WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.920
I wasn't really planning to do a segment about
this, but there have been so many bad takes

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.200
coming from [inaudible] I guess

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.720
what we're calling the revolutionary left.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:14.300
That's the non pejorative term that we've,
I guess agreed on, uh, to describe them about

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:20.500
the resignation of Bolivian president Evo
Morales that I feel compelled to discuss it

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:25.039
because the right is just completely uninformed
about Latin American politics.

00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:30.039
So I really don't have any message for them,
but there are a lot of people on the left

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:35.210
that are either misunderstanding or just wrong
in their conclusions about what has taken

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:41.050
place in Bolivia over the last, uh, close
to 15 years, calling it in completely black

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.370
and white terms, a military coup.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:49.030
So my goal here is to go through the whole
story.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.660
Hopefully this will be enlightening.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:54.149
I know I'll be called a shill and all of this
stuff, but who cares, right?

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:58.129
I mean, we, we, uh, we get one shot at doing
things the way we actually see them.

00:00:58.129 --> 00:00:59.129
You only live once.

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:02.610
And I'm going to do the stories with the nuance
that I think they deserve because that's really

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:03.610
what's missing.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:07.799
The problem is there is too much black and
white thinking in general in politics, people

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:09.299
are either good or bad.

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:11.670
The military is either good or bad.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.749
Socialism is either good or bad.

00:01:12.749 --> 00:01:18.509
A politician is either a savior or a villain,
and I know lots of people who work in the

00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:22.880
field of mental health and they tell me, you
know, a lot of the people that come in that

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.789
I see they have in their lives, all sorts
of different things going on that at their

00:01:28.789 --> 00:01:35.009
root are often caused by black and white thinking
about gray areas in life, about jobs, about

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:37.770
relationships, about their childhood, whatever.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:42.079
And I believe that the same is happening in
politics and specifically with the Bolivia

00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:43.079
situation.

00:01:43.079 --> 00:01:45.079
So let's try to put that aside.

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:47.399
Let's just all talk like reasonable people.

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:48.869
No one's shilling here.

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:51.680
Some people may be missing some of the facts.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:56.499
Some people may be coming to conclusions that
are tanged by ideology.

00:01:56.499 --> 00:02:01.450
Let's not make these umbrella black and white
declarations and let's try to actually figure

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.039
out what's going on.

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:09.840
So the Bolivian president, Evo Morales, was
first in office in 2006 a few days ago.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:16.239
He resigned at the request or demand of the
Bolivian military and request or demand we

00:02:16.239 --> 00:02:17.239
can argue about.

00:02:17.239 --> 00:02:19.490
But it's not actually the most important thing.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.650
Why did this happen a few days ago?

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:28.390
There has been rampant speculation about the
most recent election of being a bogus election.

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:34.120
The organization of American States put out
a report saying that the election results

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:41.159
were manipulated, including alterations, forced
signatures, and wide-scale data manipulation.

00:02:41.159 --> 00:02:43.880
Uh, now there is already a debate about this.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:47.680
Well, does that mean the election was bogus
or are these just reports of irregularities

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.180
like you have in many elections, including
here in the United States.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:54.530
But for me, the real story is actually bigger
than this.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.410
And I want to ask you this hypothetical.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:03:01.700
If Donald Trump during his second term, imagine
he gets reelected in November and he gets

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.120
a second term.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:08.440
Imagine that during that second term Donald
Trump change the constitution to allow a third

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:14.800
term effective immediately, but then also
claimed that since the constitution was changed,

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:20.420
his second term is sort of really his first
term under the new constitution, so he should

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.310
actually get two more.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:28.010
And then during the third term, which is really
his fourth, he loses a referendum to allow

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:35.430
unlimited terms and then his Supreme court
justices that he has selected, say, forget

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:36.609
about the term limits.

00:03:36.609 --> 00:03:38.769
You can stay as long as you want.

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:44.590
Wouldn't we in that situation as Progressive's
who are for the rule of law, wouldn't we be

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:48.540
begging someone to force Donald Trump out?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.569
Okay.

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:52.269
Now let's talk about what happened in Bolivia.

00:03:52.269 --> 00:03:57.670
Evo Morales was elected in 2006 and people
were excited because there were good things

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.799
about his election.

00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:01.290
He is not, it's not black and white.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.040
He was the first ethnically indigenous president
of Bolivia.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.040
That's great.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.209
In a country that has such a large indigenous
population.

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:11.810
Why did it take so long to have an indigenous
president? Fantastic, lovely.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:14.579
He reduced poverty during his first term.

00:04:14.579 --> 00:04:21.489
He offered a much more sensible and pragmatic
version of the socialism that has been espoused

00:04:21.489 --> 00:04:24.250
by Hugo Chavez and Nicolas Maduro.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:28.410
He invested in infrastructure and development
and grew the middle-class great, but like

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:34.639
with many of these Latin American socialists
of the last many decades, he's a an increasingly

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:35.639
authoritarian.

00:04:35.639 --> 00:04:36.730
There's corruption.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:42.780
He was elected to a five year term in 2006
he got a new constitution adopted while he

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:45.760
was president, which allowed two terms.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:52.389
Then in 2009 he called for early elections
one and said, Hey, this is sort of really

00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:56.260
like my first term because I didn't complete
the first term.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:59.889
Under the old constitution, we have a new
constitution, so I should really be able to

00:04:59.889 --> 00:05:05.840
run again in 2014 it's not objective, really
bad to change a constitution, but one should

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.849
not be allowed to stay in office longer than
they were originally supposed to because of

00:05:10.849 --> 00:05:13.169
changes made under their watch.

00:05:13.169 --> 00:05:16.259
That's what authoritarians do, so this is
already bad.

00:05:16.259 --> 00:05:20.440
He wins that early 2009 election calls it
his first term.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:26.039
So now he's allowed to run again in 2014 and
a court increasingly under his control says,

00:05:26.039 --> 00:05:28.550
yes, he is allowed to run again.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:34.000
This will count as his second term, not as
his third or his first term, not as a second.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:41.500
He wins in 2014 and then says, well, let's
do a referendum to abolish term limits altogether

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:45.270
so that I can just continue being reelected
and reelected indefinitely.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:48.509
Voters reject that referendum in Bolivia.

00:05:48.509 --> 00:05:49.860
So what does he do?

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:56.110
He appeals once again to a constitutional
court filled with people, loyal to him who

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.830
say, yep, you know what?

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.370
Running for office is a human right.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:05.310
And Bolivia term limits violate the human
rights of everyone Monarrez so he can run

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:11.270
again, which he does and wins in adult and
an election determined to have significant

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:15.050
irregularities, some characterizing it as
completely bogus.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:19.190
So listen, do I want the military to take
control of the country now?

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:20.190
Hell no.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.190
I'm from Argentina.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:23.229
I know what happens when the military takes
control.

00:06:23.229 --> 00:06:24.229
It's bad.

00:06:24.229 --> 00:06:27.509
Is this a black, white military coup?

00:06:27.509 --> 00:06:33.550
No, that's an extraordinarily myopic interpretation
that completely ignores history in Bolivia

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:39.280
for the last 13 years, if an American president
did 25% of what [inaudible] did in the election

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:43.700
system in Bolivia, we'd all be demanding their
removal.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:49.900
You'll hear comments like, well, this all
happened because American banking and finance

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.780
has ruined these countries, including Bolivia.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:56.460
How does that force the president to change
the constitution to remain in power longer

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:57.900
and how does it excuse it?

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:03.289
These things are not as cut and dry as the
revolutionary left is making them out to be.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:08.439
So my request to you is don't fall for the
black and white thinking and of course the

00:07:08.439 --> 00:07:13.720
revolutionary left will say anyone who is
not loudly opposed to this is a pro military

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:18.199
coup, pro-American interventionists, Yankee
shill.

00:07:18.199 --> 00:07:19.199
Let's be adults.

00:07:19.199 --> 00:07:20.199
Guys, give me a break.

00:07:20.199 --> 00:07:22.449
The world is not black and white the way you
make it out.

00:07:22.449 --> 00:07:23.449
Everyone.

00:07:23.449 --> 00:07:25.500
I listed some good things early in his presidency.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:26.990
He also is corrupt.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:30.490
We are also seeing a lot of the same things
happened in Bolivia that we've seen happen

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:33.949
in other places in Latin America like Venezuela
and others.

00:07:33.949 --> 00:07:40.960
When these authoritarian leaning socialists,
um, uh, remain in power for longer and longer

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.050
periods of time.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:46.580
Now interestingly, the left and right share
the existence of these factions who suffer

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:50.610
from black and white thinking on the right,
you have these libertarians and small government

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:55.490
people who think they're black and white principals
tell them everything they need to know.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.729
On the left you've got the revolutionary left
who suffers from, you know, a version of the

00:07:59.729 --> 00:08:04.030
same affliction where they see a situation
and they say, Oh yeah, the military is involved

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:06.400
and it's bad and a socialist is the president
and that's good.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.830
And he's an ethnic minority.

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:08.830
So that's, that's it.

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:11.550
That's the analysis and anything else that's
completely unacceptable.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:15.180
You're pushed out if you don't fall in line
with that ideology.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.110
Tell me all the ways I'm wrong on the facts.

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:22.800
A, I'm ready for it, but let's not play these
just completely toxic black and white games

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.009
that unfortunately are happening among a contingent
of the left.

